Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 09:52:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07983/11362] retire the inert-click pruner to the exclusion
 manifest (operator-authorised)

[outer-loop] Adds inert_click_pruner_retired_v527 to retired_extras. Operator authorised the
retirement after the 4th null; the Failed-Experiment Rerun Discipline mandates it once a
retire_if_same_verdict condition is met, and exp5756 carried one.

WHY (all measured, not asserted). Fourth attempt -- exp5595, exp5602, exp5756, and the 2026-07-26
shipped-config A/B -- returning exp5756 verdict verbatim, now with a COST rather than a bare null:
25 games x 3 seeds at budget 2000 against the SHIPPED configuration gave zero new wins on any
seed, LOST ft09 on 2 of 3 seeds (a replicated safety regression the prior attempts never saw), and
states_expanded +12.0% concentrated 93% in 3 games. The lever genuinely FIRED (147760 candidate
rows pruned), so this is not a dead-lever artifact -- which matters, because a dead lever would
warrant a wiring fix rather than retirement.

Both quantitative axes were additionally UNINTERPRETABLE rather than merely failed: capability
anchors were won by no arm so the value was arithmetically forced, and of 31 both-win cells 20 were
structurally frozen so the efficiency median pass region was EMPTY A PRIORI.

The motivating claim is FALSIFIED and that is recorded too: the pruner could never have fixed r11l,
because its inertness predicate computes changed on the RAW grid (arc_inert_click_pruner.py:217) and
r11l renders a monotone step counter, so every action is raw-frame changed and nothing can look
inert. Only the HUD/node-identity repair could fix r11l, and it did.

The entry deliberately does NOT close the whole direction. reopen_requires_new_mechanism names the
one change that would clear exp5756 bar -- a MASK-AWARE inertness predicate computing changed on the
HUD-masked grid -- with the constraint that its anchors be games the ALREADY-SHIPPED auto_hud_mask
unblocks (so a result is attributable to the predicate, not to the 2026-07-25 edge-bar repair) and
that r11l not be among them. Nav-side pruning is explicitly NOT retired by this entry.
blocked_patterns also bars citing exp5766 add:inert_click_pruner macro_delta 0.0 as causal -- its own
fields say effect_basis: exact_trace_replay_no_counterfactual_environment_delta, causal_claimed: false.

VERIFIED: manifest parses (retired 15 / retired_experiments 9 / retired_extras 37 -> 38); entry
well-formed with 4 experiment_ids and 4 blocked_patterns. exclusion_manifest_lint reports 1 HARD
violation both WITH and WITHOUT my entry -- established pre-existing by swapping HEAD manifest back
in and re-running; it concerns the conductor own roadmap scope-matching retired capstone
reconciliations, nothing to do with this entry.

